Git Task: Configure Git Hooks for Automated Release Tagging
Task Type: KodeKloud Engineer Task — Git Hook Automation

Target Server: Storage Server (ststor01) in Stratos DC

User Context: natasha

Task Overview
The Nautilus application development team needed to set up an automated release tagging mechanism for the Git repository located at /opt/cluster.git (cloned locally at /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/cluster).

The requirement was to merge the feature branch into the master branch and configure a post-update hook in the bare target repository (/opt/cluster.git). Whenever changes are pushed to the master branch, the hook automatically creates an annotated or lightweight release tag named release-YYYY-MM-DD matching the current system date.

Key Requirements
Branch Operations: Merge the feature branch into master.

Hook Setup: Create an executable post-update hook script inside /opt/cluster.git/hooks/post-update.

Tag Naming Pattern: release-YYYY-MM-DD (e.g., release-2026-10-08).

Execution User: Perform all actions as user natasha without altering existing file/directory ownerships.

Testing: Push the updated master branch to origin and verify that the release tag is generated automatically.

Implementation Steps & Script
1. Merge feature into master
Bash
cd /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/cluster
git checkout master
git merge feature
2. Configure the post-update Hook
In bare repositories (/opt/cluster.git), post-update receives modified ref names as command-line arguments ($1, $2, etc.).

Bash
cat << 'EOF' > /opt/cluster.git/hooks/post-update
#!/bin/bash

for refname in "$@"; do
  if [ "$refname" = "refs/heads/master" ]; then
    TODAY=$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
    TAG_NAME="release-$TODAY"
    
    if ! git rev-parse "$TAG_NAME" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      git tag "$TAG_NAME" HEAD
    fi
  fi
done
EOF

chmod +x /opt/cluster.git/hooks/post-update
3. Configure Git Identity & Test Push
Bash
git config --global user.email "natasha@ststor01"
git config --global user.name "natasha"

git push origin master
Verification
To verify that the hook executed successfully and generated the expected tag:

Bash
git --git-dir=/opt/cluster.git tag
Expected Output:

Plaintext
release-2026-10-08
